{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/999952-spy-games-and-joint-operations","id":999952,"title":"Spy Games and Joint Operations?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-07T14:31:19-08:00","id":999952,"title":"Spy Games and Joint Operations?","content":"yes, we all know that the experts on the spy games are the members of the T.U. But, i was wondering how does the spy game's work when it involves traditions. and how do the traditions and the technocracy see the posibility of Joint Operations in case of a bigger threat. how do each party sees the magic from the other and such","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T20:23:47-08:00","id":1000112,"title":"","content":"If the Technocrats work with Tradition mages, then it's usually under the guise of &quot;agreeing to not talk about how much they disagree with one another for as long as the task at hand takes&quot;.<br /> Joint operations between these two groups tend to be very shaky from start to end, if they don't completely fall apart mid way. <br /> The basics of it is that neither group fully trusts the other. Part of this is because Tradition mages have a hard time trusting other traditions, and the levels of paranoia that run throughout the union are staggering. So if they have a hard time trusting the devils they know, the devils they don't aren't going to have it any easier.<br /> <br /> Broadly speaking, Tradition mages will see the Technocracy as a number of things depending on the specific paradigm of the mage themselves.<br /> Primordial mages will see the Technocrats as directly harming reality, codifying it and leading the sleepers away from their potential, hammering down magic until it is nothing but cold lifeless science.<br /> Faith based mages may see the Technocracy as the very enemy of faith itself. They wish to belittle and besmirch their beliefs, harming their way of life as well as their practice in the arts.<br /> Technomancers may see the Technocrat's methods as reductive and blinkered. They refuse anything that does not fit in their plan. They blind themselves and others from the truth in order to control how sleepers think of truth.<br /> <br /> The Technocrats, on the other hand, would see mages differently depending on their level of Enlightenment.<br /> Those that are merely Extraordinary Citizens would consider mages as deluded superstitious loonies who think that the world should be brought back to the dark ages. Anything these Deviants can do has a perfectly rational explanation behind it, and the insistance that these guys have that it's Magic only demonstrates their lack of imagination or their harmful devotion to these silly myths.<br /> At low to mid levels, Reality Deviants would be considered as risks. They are capable of bending reality in dangerous ways and thus must be carefully monitored and potentially controlled. It's important they don't harm the safety of sleepers, which they are prone to do.<br /> At high levels, the Technocrats would consider these Deviants as actively going against the goals of the union. They've worked very hard at making sure reality was static and predictable for the good of all, and these guys come in here and start messing it all about. What's worse is if they start to convince sleepers that reality is malleable, everything they've done up to this point would be immediately undone. Goodbye consistency. Goodbye medical treatment, goodbye communication devices, goodbye capitalist security... This must never happen, obviously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T21:19:14-08:00","id":1000131,"title":"","content":"what about the spy games between traditions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T01:33:42-08:00","id":1000663,"title":"","content":"One good example would be the Hermetic Spy in the Keepers of the Wyck.<br /> If you haven't already I strongly recommend reading it.<br /> Saikou has a link in the signature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}